Native installer 0.11 component status

Implemented in original Zero: prepare/status/remove v1 compatibility and
new deploy SOURCE.iso LOADER.efi NEW_DIRECTORY using manifest v2.
The new directory contains verified system.iso, original16MiB storage.data,
ZEROX64.EFI and zero.install. File contents are flushed, closed, reopened and
verified before exclusive publication. No foreign runtime or helper process.

Native Linux65/65 checks PASS. Native PE under Wine53/53 checks PASS.
Evidence: installer/verification/0.11/native-{linux,wine}.json.
Private tested binaries: build/installer-0.11/zero-setup and zero-setup.exe.
Built by portability/host/durability/zero-stage2 with filesync support.
Root release integration may rebuild these using the final canonical compiler.

V2 status accepts changed structurally valid ZeroFS snapshots and preserves
all data; degraded single-snapshot status is explicit. Removal still refuses
any changed data before deleting anything. Invalid or unsupported loader
headers/sections are refused before the destination directory is created.
Linux fsync EIO injection covers each staged payload and manifest publication;
EINTR retry is also tested. Parent-directory crash durability is not claimed.

The sibling own UEFI loader reads system.iso in its firmware-visible directory.
No-CD loading and firmware path handling are verified by installer/boot/tests.
The installer does not register a firmware/BCD/GRUB entry or modify partitions.
This is not arbitrary NTFS/ext4/Btrfs Wubi boot or host-file-backed persistence.
Only the provided UEFI x64 file loader is deployed; the ISO retains separate
BIOS and IA32 boot paths. Native Windows execution and Secure Boot signing
are not verified/implemented. FNV checksums do not authenticate source files.

The finalized source/binary/loader hashes are recorded in the test reports.
The canonical OS ISO and both original user data images were unchanged by all
installer tests; every fixture used a new private directory.
